# Rolls-Royce Silver Cloud I four-door saloon, 1955-1958.
#
# The Rolls-Royce version of the same body shell as the Bentley S1: 5,384 mm
# long, 1,829 mm wide, 1,600 mm high, 3,124 mm wheelbase; 4,887 cc six with
# automatic transmission, separate chassis. 2,238 standard steel saloons built.
# The distinguishing features are the Rolls-Royce radiator and its Spirit of
# Ecstasy, the different hubcaps and badges; the body itself is shared with the
# Bentley S1, which is why this car is built from the S1 master.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Cloud
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Maroon and Grey were period Rolls-Royce finishes.
#
# Weight: 12 in total (black 5, silver 3, maroon 2, grey 2). Section F: the
# 1940s-50s class-4 row needs a British representative beside the S1.
#
# Speed 165 km/h; comfort 85/310 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1955-1958 with a road tail to about 1980.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-silver-cloud-i.blend, derived from
# citycars/4.5/bentley-s1.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rolls-royce-silver-cloud-i/ (gitignored). Images via
# Wikimedia Commons.

